  "result": "`Cart.remove('sku-1')` now removes the Widget line, and all 7 tests pass.\n\n**Root cause:** in `shop/models.py:33`, `Cart.remove` filtered lines by `l.item.name != sku`, so it compared the SKU against the item's name. `'sku-1'` never matches `'Widget'`, so nothing was removed. `Cart.add` looks lines up by `item.sku`, so the two methods disagreed.\n\n**Fix:** `remove` now filters on `l.item.sku != sku`.\n\n**Test:** I added `test_remove_by_sku` to `tests/test_pricing.py`. It builds the same cart as the demo and checks that only `sku-2` is left after the remove. I put it there because that file already tests `Cart`.\n\n**Results:** `python3 -m unittest -v` ran 7 tests and all passed, including the new one. Running `python3 -m shop.demo` now prints `1` (only the Gadget is left) instead of `2`.",
